Package: rsemverse
Type: Package
Title: Read and Prepare RSEM Gene-Level Results as Gene Symbol Tables
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Reads RSEM '*.genes.results' files listed in a sample table and
    returns a data frame of expected counts or TPM with one row per gene
    symbol and one column per sample. Symbols come from the Bioconductor
    organism annotation packages 'org.Hs.eg.db' (human) and 'org.Mm.eg.db'
    (mouse); Ensembl version suffixes are removed before the lookup and rows
    that share a symbol are summed. Further functions filter genes (the
    'edgeR' filterByExpr rule, detection thresholds, most variable genes),
    normalize between samples (CPM, TMM, upper quartile, DESeq2 median of
    ratios, quantile), transform values (log2, z-score, ranks), keep or
    remove built-in gene groups (protein-coding, mitochondrial, ribosomal,
    hemoglobin, sex-chromosome, spike-in), and return a long table joined
    with the sample information. The normalization methods give the same
    results as 'edgeR', 'DESeq2' and 'limma' without depending on them.
